From 1db212974aa0889fdc5d11b0763de4760857b091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:49:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] vulkan: FA KV-slice prefill, GQA decode kernel, decode
 tuning knobs, sparse FA on coopmat1 quantized caches

Long-context flash attention on gfx1151 (Strix Halo), measured on Laguna-S-2.1 (head dim 128, GQA 6):

- GGML_VK_FA_KV_SLICE=<tokens>: for long-KV prefill (N > 8, KV >= 2 slices, GQA <= 1 path) set split_k to
  KV / slice and make the split index the slowest part of the workgroup id (SPLIT_OUTER_BIT in
  mask_n_head_log2), so concurrently running workgroups share a cache-sized slice of K/V. FA time per
  2048-token chunk with 4096: 1054 -> 666 ms at 128K, 2471 -> 1171 ms at 245K; pp +23% at 128K end to end.
- GGML_VK_FA_DECODE_GQA=1: dedicated decode kernel (flash_attn_decode_gqa.comp) for q8_0 / q4_0 K/V, head
  dim 128, GQA 2..16: all query heads of a KV head share each K/V tile, int8 dot products against Q
  quantized per 32-block, K/V prefetched one tile ahead, split-k reduce. Faster than coopmat1 only with
  q4_0 K/V (+7% at 128K, +19% at 245K), so off by default.
- Decode knobs swept (off by default): GGML_VK_FA_SHMEM_STAGING, GGML_VK_FA_DECODE_SCALAR,
  GGML_VK_FA_DECODE_MASKOPT, GGML_VK_FA_SPLITK_WG_PER_CU, GGML_VK_FA_CM1_DECODE_SG.
- The sparse (n_kv_max) FA path is allowed on coopmat1 for quantized K/V, for block-sparse decode on a
  q8_0 cache. mask_opt skips mask rows past nem1 when bounds-checking.
- test-backend-ops: Laguna-shaped FA cases (decode, prefill, SWA, sparse at 16K-131K, long-context perf),
  top_k k=64, soft_max with a 2-D mask broadcast over 48 heads, strided mul_mat for the block bounds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
